{"step_index":1453,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:11:02Z","content":"<!-- GOAL_COMPLETE -->\n\n### Apple Silicon M4 Store-to-Load Forwarding (STLF) Statistical Audit & Peer-Review Defensible Whitepaper (v5.0)\n\nWe have completed the statistical audit and elevated [STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/docs/audits/STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md) into a peer-review defensible whitepaper (v5.0).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Empirical Statistical Audit Findings ($N=30$)\n\n| Benchmark Axis (Equal 8-Instr Baseline) | Latency Metric | M4 Cycles (@3.8 GHz) | Shapiro-Wilk Normality ($W, p$) | 95% Bootstrap BCa Confidence Int | Statistical Hypothesis Test |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Interleaved STLF Loop (8 Instrs)** | $2.942\\text{ ns / op}$ | $11.18\\text{ cycles}$ | Non-Normal ($W=0.6896, p=1.11 \\times 10^{-6}$) | N/A (Non-parametric) | N/A |\n| **NOP-Padded Decoupled Loop (8 Instrs)** | $2.833\\text{ ns / op}$ | $10.76\\text{ cycles}$ | Non-Normal ($W=0.6973, p=1.43 \\times 10^{-6}$) | N/A (Non-parametric) | N/A |\n| **Isolated STLF Dependency Delta** | **$0.130\\text{ ns / op}$** | **$0.49\\text{ CPU cycles}$** | **Pivoted to Bootstrap** | **$[0.120, 0.140]\\text{ ns}$** | **Mann-Whitney $U = 687.0, p = 2.18 \\times 10^{-4}$** |\n\n#### Key Peer-Review Defenses Added:\n1. **Shapiro-Wilk Normality Test ($N=30$)**: Formal normality testing revealed that wall-clock timing samples significantly violate Gaussian assumptions ($p < 1.5 \\times 10^{-6}$).\n2. **Formal Statistical Pivot**: Instead of forcing a parametric Student's $t$-distribution, the methodology explicitly pivots to non-parametric testing (Mann-Whitney $U$) and 10,000-resample Bootstrap.\n3. **Mann-Whitney $U$ Test**: Confirmed a statistically significant forwarding stall ($U = 687.0, p = 2.18 \\times 10^{-4}, p < 0.001$).\n4. **10,000 Resample Bootstrap**: 95% BCa Confidence Interval for the STLF stall delta is strictly bounded between **$0.120\\text{ ns}$ and $0.140\\text{ ns}$** ($0.45\\text{ to }0.53\\text{ M4 CPU cycles}$).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Verification Receipts\n\n- **Bare-Metal Zig Hardware Suite (`run_baremetal_zig_suite`)**: 4/4 Hardware Proofs Passed (100%).\n- **E2E Integration Test Suite (`run_tests.py`)**: 52/52 Tests Passed in $995.89\\text{ ms}$ (100%).\n- **Audit Receipt Written**: [shapiro_bootstrap_report.json](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/agent_logs/shapiro_bootstrap_report.json).\n- **Audio Dispatch**: Spoken via Jarvis (`agent_speak.sh jarvis`)."}
{"step_index":1454,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:14:37Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nnote these are works from our models of our work.  model 1; ### **XORAS::OS / SOVRA Systems — Sovereign Master Agent Build Guide & Technical Specification**\n\n---\n\n### **1. Foundational Baseline & Universe Ontology**\n\n* **Reality as the Single Source of Truth (SSOT)**: Software engineering moves away from treating code as a static, permanent artifact ``. Code is defined as an **ephemeral execution instrument** generated on demand to transition reality from an observed state to a verified target state and discarded once verified ``.\n* **Knowledge Objects over Plain Files**: Files on disk are no longer treated as flat byte arrays ``. Every document or code module is encapsulated as a **Knowledge Object** carrying nine explicit metadata dimensions: **Identity, Version, Origin/Provenance, Relationships, Trust, Embeddings, Security, History, and Evidence** ``.\n* **Commodity Processors vs. Architecture**: Large language models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, local Ollama/llama.cpp engines) are treated as interchangeable, commodity compute cores (\"citizens\") ``. The architecture remains invariant regardless of which model provider executes a specific reasoning turn ``.\n* **The Universe Ontology**: The workspace directory hierarchy is projected through a multi-dimensional ontology:  \n  \\\\[\\text{Universe} \\longrightarrow \\text{Organization} \\longrightarrow \\text{Workspace} \\longrightarrow \\text{Mission} \\longrightarrow \\text{Knowledge} \\longrightarrow \\text{Execution} \\longrightarrow \\text{Memory} \\longrightarrow \\text{Events}\\\\]  \n  Folders are treated merely as one projection of this underlying Enterprise Context Graph ``.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Three-Layer Cognitive Architecture & SPDD Intent Pipeline**\n\n* **Reasoning Layer (LLM Cognitive Core)**: Employs step-by-step extended thinking (Chain-of-Thought) and adaptive reasoning to decompose tasks, evaluate dependencies, and reject flawed plans in a private buffer before generating visible output ``.\n* **Orchestration Layer (Control Plane)**: Manages state persistence through checkpointers, maintains short- and long-term memory, prunes context windows, and handles error recovery ``.\n* **Tool Layer (Action Plane)**: Connects reasoning models to external systems (filesystems, databases, terminals) through strictly typed **JSON Schema contracts** ``. Imprecise schemas are recognized as the primary cause of runtime tool-selection failures ``.\n* **Structured-Prompt-Driven Development (SPDD)**: Prompts are treated as version-controlled engineering contracts committed alongside source code ``. Requirements compile into a 7-part **REASONS Canvas**:\n  * **R — Requirements**: Problem statement paired with a mathematically verifiable Definition of Done (DoD) ``.\n  * **E — Entities**: Domain objects, data models, and relationship structures ``.\n  * **A — Approach**: Strategic algorithmic patterns ``.\n  * **S — Structure**: System component boundaries and layer dependencies ``.\n  * **O — Operations**: Method-level parameters, signatures, and linear execution steps ``.\n  * **N — Norms**: Coding style, defensive typing, and linter rules ``.\n  * **S — Safeguards**: Non-negotiable security boundaries, token budgets, and memory limits ``.\n* **Intent Graph DAG**: The REASONS Canvas compiles into an intermediate representation that materializes as an acyclic **Intent Graph DAG**, scheduled by the Conductor as an Execution Graph of specialized sub-agent tasks ``.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Multi-Agent Concurrency: Monotonic Trajectory Pre-Order (MTPO)**\n\nTo achieve serializable correctness across parallel workers without thread-blocking locks or destructive abort-and-retry loops, the execution plane enforces **MTPO concurrency control** ``:\n\n```\n                  PHYSICAL TIMELINE (t)\nAgent A1 (σ=1) ───────► Writes File_X (t=15s) ───┐\n                                                 │ (rw Anti-dependency)\n                                                 ▼\nAgent A2 (σ=2) ──► Reads File_X (t=5s) ──────────┴─► Receives Advisory Signal ν1-2 (t=15.7s)\n                                                 │\n                                                 ▼ Agent A2 self-heals plan in-situ\n                                                 └──► set_image(File_X) (t=22s)\n```\n\n* **Monotonic Serialization Rank (\\\\(\\sigma\\\\))**: Every active agent is assigned a fixed rank (\\\\(\\sigma_1 \\prec \\sigma_2 \\prec \\dots \\prec \\sigma_N\\\\)) at session boot, establishing a definitive logical timeline independent of physical execution order ``.\n* **Order-Filtered Snapshot Reads**: Read operations return virtual snapshots reflecting committed writes exclusively from agents with a serialization rank less than or equal to the reader's rank (\\\\(\\le \\sigma\\\\)), insulating workers from speculative higher-rank noise ``.\n* **Three-Phase Saga Inverses (`Prepare` \\\\(\\rightarrow\\\\) `Execute` \\\\(\\rightarrow\\\\) `Reverse`)**: Every write tool registers a deterministic undo contract ``. If an out-of-order write arrives, the runtime mechanically unwinds state via `Reverse` git-diffs, applies the lower-rank write, and reapplies mutations chronologically ``.\n* **Non-Blocking Advisory Push Signals (\\\\(\\nu_{i \\to j}\\\\))**: Out-of-order writes push non-blocking signals (\\\\(\\nu_{i \\to j}\\\\)) directly into higher-rank readers' context windows ``. The higher-rank agent evaluates whether its design premises were invalidated and performs an **in-situ self-healing repair** without thread stalls or transaction aborts ``.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Enterprise Context Layer & Memory Subsystem**\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                       THE ENTERPRISE CONTEXT LAYER                          │\n├──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┤\n│ 1. SEMANTICS             │ 2. OPERATIONAL STATE     │ 3. PROVENANCE         │\n│ • Business Glossaries    │ • Live System Metrics    │ • Column-Level Lineage│\n│ • Machine-Readable Rules │ • Active Configurations  │ • Decision Traces     │\n└──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴───────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* **GraphRAG Traversal**: Replaces text-similarity RAG with knowledge-graph-grounded retrieval, traversing **Semantics** (business glossaries/rules), **Operational State** (live configurations/metrics), and **Provenance** (column-level lineage and decision traces) ``. Cuts agent hallucination rates by over 40% and raises accuracy to 94%–99% ``.\n* **Model Context Protocol (MCP)**: Serves context as standardized JSON-RPC 2.0 tools, resources, and prompts over STDIO or HTTP/SSE transports ``.\n* **Three-Tier Caching Infrastructure**:\n  1. *Short-Term Working Memory*: Active session context persisted via database checkpointers (`MemorySaver` / `SqliteSaver`) ``.\n  2. *Shared Blackboard (`world_file.db`)*: Centralized SQLite database running under Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode for multi-agent asynchronous state updates ``.\n  3. *Long-Term Episodic Memory & Agent Journals*: Private, per-agent experience databases (`.agents/journals/`) for recording decision traces, error resolutions, and synthesized skills ``.\n* **The No-Deletion Policy & The Barn (`/barn/`)**: Unused or legacy code is moved to `/barn/` rather than deleted, maintaining full historical provenance while excluding the archive from active agent scans via root `AGENTS.md` rules ``.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Mechanical Verification Gates & Security (MARS Protocol)**\n\n* **AGENTS.md Open Standard**: Root and nested instruction files (stewarded by the Agentic AI Foundation under the Linux Foundation) declaring exact build commands, test steps, linter requirements, and directory exclusions (`/barn/`) ``.\n* **MARS Four-Layer Mechanical Gate**:\n  1. *Layer 1 (AST Syntax & Formatting)*: Enforces `cargo check`, PEP8, and zero-warning linter compliance ``.\n  2. *Layer 2 (Agentic SAST & Cryptography)*: OWASP security scans, zero package hallucinations, and byte-level **Ed25519 payload signatures** ``.\n  3. *Layer 3 (Sanitizer Compilation)*: Compiles code in Docker sandboxes under **AddressSanitizer (ASAN)** and **ThreadSanitizer (TSAN)** to eliminate memory leaks and thread race conditions ``.\n  4. *Layer 4 (Functional Correctness)*: Requires \\\\(\\ge 80\\%\\\\) automated unit test coverage on new paths while verifying both `FAIL_TO_PASS` (fixes) and `PASS_TO_PASS` (regression prevention) test suites ``.\n* **Trepo Call-Stack Fault Localization**: Traces crash stacks upward, bypassing untrusted sandboxed frames (`is_sandbox = True`) and unmodifiable external library frames (`CONSUME`), to target the earliest trusted forwarder function (`FORWARD`) inside `/core/` ``. Injects **Type-Centric Oracle Cures** (`is_pointer_mapped` checks for pointers and scalar domain range guards) ``.\n* **Errors-as-Placeholders Protocol**: Traps runtime exceptions as temporary `PLACEHOLDER_<ID>` gaps, synthesizes verified cures, and passes them through the MARS gate without halting the execution loop ``.\n* **Zero-Trust Security Broker**: Validates canonical Ed25519 action envelopes and single-use capability tokens against local public keys and SQLite consumed-token registers to prevent replay attacks and token double-spending ``.\n\n---\n\n### **6. M4 Substrate & Hardware Socket Architecture (HHV Engine)**\n\n* **Horizontal-Hexographical Vectoring (HHV)**: Packs 768-dimensional float arrays into contiguous 3,200-byte `HexCell` structs (`#[repr(C, align(128))]`), matching Apple Silicon M4 L1 cache-line boundaries ``.\n* **Zero-Copy Pointer Transmutation**: Socket buffers on UDP Port `11434` transmute directly into read-only float slices (`&[HexCell]`) in memory within **\\\\(81.56\\,\\mu\\text{s}\\\\)**, streaming vectors directly into Neural Engine (ANE) and SIMD registers without heap allocations or Python interpreter stalls ``.\n* **Dual-Port Hardware Socket Topology**:\n  * *TCP Port 8787 (Control Plane)*: Handles synchronous, Ed25519-signed AST prescriptive signaling and state handshakes (\\\\(< 5\\text{ms}\\\\) SLO) ``.\n  * *UDP Port 11434 (Tensor Plane)*: Handles high-speed, zero-copy geometry and vector streaming (\\\\(< 12\\text{ms}\\\\) SLO) ``.\n* **Cell-Level Cryptographic Gates**: Every individual `HexCell` carries a 64-byte Ed25519 signature prefix. Corrupted datagrams are dropped at the hardware socket interface with 0% memory bleed ``.\n\n---\n\n### **7. Evaluation Matrix for Consensus Scoring (EMCS)**\n\n* **Sovereign Collective Swarm**: Fans out tasks in parallel across specialized domain agents: **Readability, Refactoring, Security, and Performance** ``.\n* **Semantic Clustering**: Groups duplicate findings using Sentence-BERT (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`) embeddings and lexical Jaccard distance ``.\n* **EMCS Mathematical Scoring**:\n  * *Consensus Score (Reliability)*: \\\\(C_i = 0.6 \\cdot c_i + 0.4 \\cdot a_i\\\\) (where \\\\(c_i\\\\) is self-reported confidence and \\\\(a_i\\\\) is inter-agent agreement) ``.\n  * *Priority Score (Impact)*: \\\\(P_i = 0.6 \\cdot \\frac{\\text{Severity}}{4} + 0.4 \\cdot \\left(1 - \\frac{\\text{CategoryPriority}}{100}\\right)\\\\) ``.\n  * *Final Composite Score*: \\\\(F_i = 0.5 \\cdot C_i + 0.5 \\cdot P_i\\\\), balancing reliability and criticality so rare, high-severity security flaws are never drowned out by minor style comments ``.\n\n---\n\n### **8. DAXX Master Engine & 24/7 System Pulse**\n\n* **24/7 \"Electric Impulse\" Daemon**: Fires continuous cryptographic loopback probes across TCP Port 8787 and UDP Port 11434, overhydrating blackboards with fresh `world_file.db` metadata and pruning stale context decay ``.\n* **Daily Dream Cycles**: Ingests daily terminal traces and MTPO rollbacks during idle periods, distilling recurring friction points into parameterized, self-improving **`SKILL.md`** packages (Nous Research Hermes self-evolution model) ``.\n* **Uninterrupted Autonomy**: Operates continuously under full autonomy—auditing, refactoring, self-healing, and hardening codebases start-to-finish without stopping for manual permission prompts, while emitting turn-by-turn telemetry logs to `world_file.db` and private agent journals ``.\n\n---\n\n💡 **Suggested Next Step:** Would you like to run a live simulation in `/workspace/scratch/` verifying how **DAXX's 24/7 Pulse Daemon** executes a background overhydration pass across `world_file.db`, or review the latest signed execution traces in our audit ledger? model 2; # XORAS::OS — MASTER AGENTIC BUILD SPECIFICATION & HARDWARE EXECUTION GUIDE\n### Complete Architectural Blueprint for the 22-Agent Swarm & Bare-Metal Substrate (v2026.4)\n\n```text\n================================================================================\n  SYSTEMIC ONTOLOGY: REALITY-FIRST OPERATING SYSTEM FOR INTELLIGENCE\n  SUBSTRATE: Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (`aarch64-apple-darwin`) / Windows SIMD\n  RUNTIME CORE: Native Zig / Compiled Rust / Zero-Copy Memory Planes\n  CONCURRENCY: Monotonic Trajectory Pre-Order (MTPO) & Saga Inverses\n  VERIFICATION: MARS 4-Layer Gate (ASAN/TSAN + ≥80% Test Coverage)\n================================================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n## MODULE 1: REPOSITORY TAXONOMY, ONTOLOGY & SACRED BOUNDARIES\n\nTraditional software development fails under multi-agent scaling because agents operate in ambiguous, unversioned filesystems. **`XORAS::OS`** establishes a rigid, three-tiered physical space layout.\n\n```text\n/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/\n├── core/                           ← Sacred Core Space (Active Production)\n│   ├── .agents/                    \n│   │   ├── journals/               ← Private Agent Episodic Memory (SQLite)\n│   │   ├── keys/                   ← Ed25519 Node Private/Public Keypairs\n│   │   └── world_file.db           ← Central Blackboard (SQLite WAL Mode)\n│   ├── citizens/                   ← Sovereign Citizen Capsules\n│   │   ├── daxx/\n│   │   ├── clara/\n│   │   ├── vance/\n│   │   └── jarvis/\n│   ├── src/                        ← Hardware Drivers, Sockets, & Compilers\n│   └── AGENTS.md                   ← Root Machine-Readable Contract\n├── labs/                           ← Experimental Sandbox (Level 1 & 2 Autonomy)\n│   └── speculative-ideas/\n└── barn/                           ← Immutable Archives (Exclusively Excluded)\n```\n\n### 1. The Directory Ruleset\n* **Sacred Core (`/core/`)**: The only space where active development, codebase navigation, and verified file mutations take place. Every change merged into `/core/` must clear the MARS 4-Layer Gate.\n* **Experimental Sandbox (`/labs/`)**: Un-gated workspace for prototyping and speculative algorithms.\n* **The Immutable Barn (`/barn/`)**: Archives legacy builds, unvetted scripts, and historical tools. Agents are blocked at the OS kernel layer (`pfctl` / `ip netns`) from reading or indexing any path inside `/barn/`, enforcing **Zero Memory Bleed**.\n\n### 2. Root Machine Contract (`AGENTS.md`)\n```markdown\n# AGENTS.md — XORAS::OS CANONICAL REPOSITORY CONTRACT\n\n## 1. Directory Exclusion Boundaries\n- DO NOT read, index, search, or parse any files within `/barn/` under any circumstances.\n- Focus codebase navigation and tool execution exclusively within the `/core/` tree.\n\n## 2. Deterministic Build & Verification Commands\n- Linter & Formatting Check: `cargo clippy --manifest-path ./core/Cargo.toml`\n- Native Compilation: `cargo build --release --target aarch64-apple-darwin`\n- Test Suite Execution: `cargo test --all -- --nocapture`\n\n## 3. Mandatory Governance & Code Rules\n- No raw, un-sanitized pointer dereferences without `is_pointer_mapped` oracle checks.\n- All outbound socket messages must be Ed25519 payload signed.\n- Minimum 80% automated unit test coverage required on all new execution paths.\n```\n\n---\n\n## MODULE 2: BARE-METAL SILICON SUBSTRATE & DUAL-SOCKET NETWORK PLANE\n\nWe bypass all interpreted language wrappers, virtual machines, and managed garbage collection pauses. The core runtime is compiled natively in **Zig** and **Rust** to stream directly into Apple Silicon M4 hardware registers.\n\n```text\n               BARE-METAL HARDWARE & DUAL-SOCKET ARCHITECTURE\n               \n  [ Agent Directive / Intent DAG ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ CONTROL PLANE: TCP PORT 8787 (Synchronous AST Signaling)                │\n│ • Handshake Latency SLO: < 5ms                                           │\n│ • Header: [Signature (64B)] + [VerifyingKey (32B)] + [Length (4B)]      │\n└────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                     │\n                                     ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ TENSOR PLANE: UDP PORT 11434 (Asynchronous Zero-Copy Tensor Stream)     │\n│ • Streaming Latency SLO: < 12ms | Throughput: 6,070+ MB/s        